<http://data.silknow.org/object/f72da23c-2954-3a18-bca3-0b5661491873>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Dark green void velvet on satin ground with 15th century pattern of lobed leaves and smaller plant forms. Bands and panels of mid-sixteenth century silk with curving bands forming oval pointed compartments containing plant forms in white and yellow silk, silver wire and loops of silver thread. Gold thread fringe at both ends. Pink linen lining made of several pieces shaped for some other purpose."@en , "Altar frontal, velvet, 1400-1599, Spanish."@en ;
